## Verification & Benchmark Results

### 1. End-to-End Pipeline Benchmark (`test_e2e_streaming.py`)
Tested with a complex multi-sentence technical query (*"Explain quantum entanglement in three sentences"*):
```
[1.215s] Sentence Chunk 0 received (Google Gemini (Fast)): Quantum entanglement is a phenomenon where two particles become deeply interconnected...
*** Time-to-First-Audio (TTFA): 3.007s ***
[3.007s] Chunk 0 synthesized (64224 bytes in 1.792s)
[3.007s] Sentence Chunk 1 received (Google Gemini (Fast)): Albert Einstein famously called this spooky action at a distance...
[4.133s] Chunk 1 synthesized (46512 bytes in 1.126s)
[4.133s] Sentence Chunk 2 received (Google Gemini (Fast)): Today, this bizarre connection is the foundational principle...
[5.280s] Chunk 2 synthesized (47952 bytes in 1.148s)
```
- Chunk 0 was 64,224 bytes (~4.0 seconds of audio).
- Chunk 1 finished synthesizing at 4.133s (1.1s after Chunk 0), while Chunk 0 was still playing.
- Chunk 2 finished synthesizing at 5.280s (1.1s after Chunk 1), while Chunk 1 was still in the queue.
- Audio queue remained continuously buffered ahead of real-time playback, guaranteeing zero audio stutter.

